AWS inventory with bounded API collection, SQLite SQL, and FalkorDB snapshots

Usage: aws-inventory <COMMAND>

Commands:
  catalog       List implemented resource tables and API operations
  coverage      Inspect reviewed collection coverage and exclusions for all pinned AWS schemas
  plan          Inspect the collection stages and bounds without loading AWS credentials
  sdk-catalog   Inspect pinned official SDK versions; this is separate from collector coverage
  demo          Create a clearly synthetic, reproducible local demonstration
  ingest        Ingest CollectionEvent JSONL; exact page replay is safe
  export        Stream a finalized inventory snapshot, including coverage, to JSON or JSONL
  deliver       Export an existing scan and optionally project it to FalkorDB without recollecting AWS
  query         Read-only SQLite SQL; result count and execution work are bounded
  report        Summarize a scan and include explicit coverage/failure information
  architecture  Summarize finalized topology, routes, load balancers and unresolved references
  diff          Compare finalized snapshots without treating missing observations as deletion
  neighbors     Traverse bounded declared configuration relationships around a resource
  path          Find a bounded relationship path; this is not a network reachability test
  findings      Report evidence-backed architecture observations with explicit uncertainty
  discover      Discover existing organization accounts and inventory sources (requires aws feature)
  job           Persist, inspect, cancel and execute bounded scan jobs
  graph-export  Build a bounded JSONL plan of idempotent FalkorDB graph writes
  graph-push    Apply a graph plan, committing local checkpoints only after server ACKs
  scan          Collect AWS configuration metadata using existing credentials (requires aws feature)
  help          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
